    {
      "tableId": "detachment-huron-s-marauders:rule:table:1",
      "source": {
        "document": "books/chaos-space-marines/sources/waha-11e-current-2026-09-29/chaos-space-marines.html",
        "sha256": "54e028296c063629f43e82a9aba26943568dee3ae819e36620f72dec47529c4e",
        "selector": "//*[@id=\"Tyrannical-Motivation\"]/parent::div/div[contains(@class,\"BreakInsideAvoid\")][1]//table"
      },
      "cells": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "/rows/0/0",
          "rowSpan": 1,
          "columnSpan": 1,
          "header": false,
          "displayValue": "Huron’s Elite\n\nHand-picked by Huron Blackheart himself, these warriors strive to retain his favour with feats of arms.\n\nEach time a model in this unit makes an attack, add 1 to the Hit roll."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tableId": "detachment-huron-s-marauders:rule:table:2",
      "source": {
        "document": "books/chaos-space-marines/sources/waha-11e-current-2026-09-29/chaos-space-marines.html",
        "sha256": "54e028296c063629f43e82a9aba26943568dee3ae819e36620f72dec47529c4e",
        "selector": "//*[@id=\"Tyrannical-Motivation\"]/parent::div/div[contains(@class,\"BreakInsideAvoid\")][2]//table"
      },
      "cells": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "/rows/0/0",
          "rowSpan": 1,
          "columnSpan": 1,
          "header": false,
          "displayValue": "Mobile Marauders\n\nThe Red Corsairs utilise a highly mobile form of warfare and, under Huron’s watch, are relentless in their aggression.\n\nThis unit is eligible to shoot and declare a charge in a turn in which it Fell Back.\n\nDesigner’s Note: If a unit is gaining eligibility to shoot and declare a charge in a turn in which it Fell Back as a result of being visible to Huron Blackheart, but after making a Fall Back move it is no longer visible to Huron Blackheart, that unit will not be eligible to shoot in your Shooting phase or to declare a charge in your Charge phase unless it is visible again at the start of the respective phase."
        }
      ]
    }
